## Step 1 — Write the behavioural contract ("the paper"), committed FIRST

Land `repos/system_upgrade/common/actors/targetuserspacecreator/CONTRACT.md` as the first commit
(commit order is itself the proof the redesign was spec-first). If maintainers object to an in-actor
`.md`, the fallback is `docs/source/` or the PR body — the load-bearing requirement is that it is
committed before any logic-redesign commit.

The contract describes outside-observable behaviour (internal names irrelevant), reorganising §C from
"inventory of old code" into "spec a fresh author implements from". Sections:

1. Purpose & placement (phase `TargetTransactionFactsPhaseTag`; effective order relative to
   `createisorepofile` → this actor → `swapdistropackagesworkaround`).
2. Inputs consumed + validation/hard-stop rules (no `RHSMInfo` & not `skip_rhsm`; `skip_rhsm` &
   `RHSMInfo` present; no `StorageInfo`).
3. Outputs produced + every downstream consumer and the fields it reads (this section records the
   renamed-model decision + rationale).
4. Ordering guarantees other actors may depend on.
5. Scratch / overlay / nspawn / conditional ISO-mount setup.
6. Content-access establishment in scratch (RHUI client swap R1–R7; RHSM container-mode + cert
   switch; CentOS `$stream` var; custom repofile install).
7. Repository discovery & selection (distro/RHUI/all repoid discovery; base-repo skip conditions).
8. The five inhibitor conditions (trigger, severity, groups, key/title, remediation): missing
   product cert; duplicate repos (skip_rhsm only); missing base repos; no enabled repos; missing
   custom repos.
9. Userspace build (wipe/recreate, bind-mount, gpg import, dnf install, cert/repo access, copy
   files, leapp plugin, RHUI post-cleanup, container mode).
10. dnf install command shape + the **four** failure-hint branches (disk-space→KB; proxy-in-dnf.conf;
    proxy-in-repo; CentOS→RHEL target-version).
11. Cert/repo access; **mark `/etc/pki` decoupling as CARVE-OUT (frozen)**.
12. Env-var switches (`LEAPP_CONTAINER_ROOT`, `LEAPP_DEVEL_USE_PERSISTENT_PACKAGE_CACHE`,
    `LEAPP_NO_RHSM`, `LEAPP_NOGPGCHECK`, target/product-type overrides).
13. RHUI invariants R1–R7 (verbatim acceptance gate).

