## Definition of done (gates) — reframed

**Gates (must pass):**
1. Behavioural equivalence: CONTRACT.md items pass a documented contract-walk; §B interface unchanged
   except the deliberate model rename; all five inhibitors + R1–R7 hold; the behaviour-anchored
   safety-net suite passes unchanged; el8 + el9 containers green.
2. Spec-first proof: CONTRACT.md committed before any logic-redesign commit (commit order).
3. Each named god function decomposed into individually-tested units (reviewer checks the Step-3 map).
4. Structural: cycle resolved with zero function-local imports; `constants.py` gone;
   renamed-model rationale written; **TODO/FIXME in the actor libs = 0** except explicitly-annotated
   out-of-scope shared-lib notes (e.g. the rhsm dup-inhibitor).
5. Coverage rises where it was zero (dnf assembly/diagnosis, `prep_repository_access`, RHUI repoid
   discovery, the previously-skipped gather test).
6. Readability: a maintainer can read `perform()` top-to-bottom and see the contract's control flow.

**Non-gating diagnostics (report, don't gate):** per-module `git diff -M` (excluding the carve-out)
as a review smell — a module that looks like a pure rename is a flag to investigate. Net-LOC as an
observation in the PR description; note it may *rise* where tests/docstrings/splits were added.
_Rationale: LOC-falls and diff-not-clean are similarity proxies — the same class of metric that
caused the first failure, and they contradict the frozen carve-out._

